-- Data.Vendors: vendors whose window was opened in game, as IDs and map
-- positions only (the Lab's vendor recorder, build 70391; /recollect-data
-- rebuilds this file). A position is where the player stood when the window
-- opened, on that map (x and y from 0 to 1); vendors the Lab has not recorded
-- stand where AllTheThings places them. An NPC may have several places, ";"
-- between them, the first its place for a waypoint. An object with map 0 has no
-- known position (no waypoint). S holds the container object a treasure's
-- spawn is filed under (AllTheThings). items is what each vendor sells, uncapped, for
-- curator mode: the item codes' sellers, purchases and recorded trades (gold-only
-- ones too), leaving out what every source says is no longer sold there. Its
-- order is the index a curator's confirmation counts over, so it holds only for
-- this data version. dataVersion and format are the data build's stamp;
-- Relations.lua and Hints.lua carry the same one.
